    "group": "narrative",
    "fact": "three_pigs",
    "prompt": "Tell the traditional story of the Three Little Pigs in about 180 words, from the beginning to the ending.",
    "max_new_tokens": 256,
    "response": "In ancient times, there was a village where pigs lived happily. One day, a big wolf came and said that he would eat all the piglets if they didn't give him their food. The villagers were very sad because they had no food for themselves.\n\nThe next morning, the villagers decided to build a house with sticks and mud. They wanted to protect themselves from the wolf's attack. Then, they built a wall around the house using stones and bricks. The villagers also made some wooden fences to keep out the wolves.\n\nOne day, the wolf came again and ate everything in the village. The villagers were so angry that they decided to fight back. They used their sticks and stones to beat the wolf and scare it away.\n\nAfterward, the villagers built another house with more materials. They added more walls and fences to make sure everyone could stay safe. They also planted trees and flowers to beautify the area.\n\nFrom then on, the villagers lived happily ever after, protected by their houses and surrounded by greenery. The Three Little Pigs never got hungry again, and they learned that even though they might be small, they could still defend themselves and protect others.",
